# `~/.config` is a real directory, not a symlink to this package, so live
# credentials no longer sit in this working tree. Adding a new config here is
# therefore an ordinary `git add` -- there is no allowlist to extend.
#
# What remains is a backstop. Each of these lived here before the restructure,
# and a folded package directory on a fresh install could route a tool's writes
# back into the repo. If one reappears, it is a mistake, not a commit.

# Credentials
1Password/
gh/config.yml
gh/hosts.yml
op/
creds/*
!creds/README.md

# Machine-local overrides (templates are the tracked `.example` files)
dotfiles/local.zsh
dotfiles/local.fish
dotfiles/api_tokens.zsh

# Tool-written state
homebrew/trust.json.lock
nvim/lazy-lock.json
*.sock
